set-jump: post_election

@post_election
on-arrival: {!
// set congress proportion to votes
Q.pvda_r = Q.pvda_votes;
Q.cda_r = Q.cda_votes;
Q.sp_r = Q.sp_votes;
Q.d66_r = Q.d66_votes;
Q.vvd_r = Q.vvd_votes;
Q.pvv_r = Q.pvv_votes;
Q.gl_r = Q.gl_votes;
Q.other_r = Q.other_votes;

// The largest party can only be the gl or the pvda.
Q.largest_party = 'pvda';
if (Q.gl_r >= Q.pvda_r && Q.gl_r >= Q.sp_r) {
    Q.largest_party = 'gl';
}
if (Q.sp_r >= Q.pvda_r && Q.sp_r >= Q.gl_r) {
    Q.largest_party = 'sp';
}

// coalitions
Q.weimar_coalition = Q.pvda_r + Q.d66_r + Q.cda_r - 3;
Q.grand_coalition = Q.pvda_r + Q.d66_r + Q.cda_r + Q.vvd_r;
Q.bourgeois_coalition = Q.d66_r + Q.cda_r + Q.vvd_r + Q.other_r;
Q.center_right_coalition = Q.cda_r + Q.d66_r + Q.vvd_r + Q.other_r + Q.pvv_r;
Q.right_coalition = Q.cda_r + Q.vvd_r + Q.other_r + Q.pvv_r;
Q.far_right_coalition = Q.pvv_r + Q.gl_r;
Q.left_coalition = Q.pvda_r + Q.sp_r;
// this is an absurd concept lol
Q.united_front_coalition = Q.pvda_r + Q.sp_r + Q.cda_r + Q.d66_r - 3;
Q.anti_democratic_coalition = Q.sp_r + Q.gl_r;
// aka everyone except nacdai, sp, pvv
Q.neo_weimar_coalition = Q.pvda_r + Q.d66_r + Q.cda_r + Q.vvd_r + Q.other_r;
!}

The electoral system is essentially proportional, with the proportion of Reichstag seats roughly equal to the proportion of votes.
 
**Election results:**

# 1928: 30, 1930: 25, 1932: 22
pvda: [+ pvda_r +]

# 1928: 15, 1930: 15, 1932: 
cda + BVP: [+ cda_r +]

# 1928: 10, 1930: 13
sp: [+ sp_r +]

# 1928: 5, 1930: 4 (as DstP)
d66: [+ d66_r +]

# 1928: 9, 1930: 5
vvd: [+ vvd_r +]

# 1928: 14, 1930: 7
pvv: [+ pvv_r +]

# 1928: 3, 1930: 18
gl: [+ gl_r +]

# 1928: 9, 1930: 10
Other: [+ other_r +]

**Potential coalitions:**

Weimar Coalition (pvda + cda + d66): [+ weimar_coalition +]

Grand Coalition (pvda + cda + BVP + d66 + vvd): [+ grand_coalition +]

Bourgeois Coalition (cda + BVP + d66 + vvd + Others): [+ bourgeois_coalition +]

Right-wing Coalition (cda + BVP + vvd + Others + pvv): [+ right_coalition +]

